				{
					"kind": "class",
					"name": "FMjpegAviWriter",
					"namespace": "Mowo",
					"doc": "Motion-JPEG in an AVI 1.0 container: every frame an independent JPEG, an\nidx1 index, nothing else. It is the one video format that needs no codec\nlibrary to write and that every player and editing tool opens, so it is the\nfallback on a host without an OS encoder for the MP4 output. AVI 1.0 caps a\nRIFF at 1 GiB, so a frame that would cross it is refused rather than written\ninto a file no reader will accept; a long render goes to MP4.",
